course: dictionary
lesson: 7808
title: Old words with strange meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some old books use words that mean something different today. The best clue is the sentence around the word. Read the whole sentence and ask: what meaning would make sense here?
explain: In Alice in Wonderland, Alice has seen a cat vanish and a baby turn into a pig. «She was getting so used to queer things happening.» Those things are strange, so queer must mean strange. Swap in strange and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and some meanings are not kind. Today, use queer only in its old meaning, or about people in the way they choose to be described. Never use it to tease or hurt anyone.
fact: «Queer» (old-fashioned) means strange or odd.
fact: In old books, «queer» can also mean unwell, as in «I feel queer».
fact: Some people use «queer» to describe themselves, and many people accept this today.
fact: For a long time «queer» was an insult against gay people, and it can still hurt, so never use it to mock anyone.
fact: The same word can be harmless in an old story and hurtful today, so think about who you are talking to.
exercise: «The animals heard queer sounds in the Wild Wood.» What does queer mean here? | *Strange or odd | Soft and fluffy | Warm and sunny | Loud and cheerful
exercise: Ella says, «I feel queer» after the bumpy car ride. What does queer mean? | Sleepy | Hungry | Excited | *Unwell, not feeling well
exercise: «She was getting so used to queer things happening.» Find and copy one word that means the same as queer here. | getting | *strange | happening | things
test: Why should you be careful when using queer today? | It means exactly the same as strange, so it can never hurt anyone | *It was once used as an insult, and it can still hurt people | It only means tired | It is always a word for food
test: What is a good way to check the meaning of an unknown word? | Count the letters in the word | Skip the sentence and never come back | Guess the longest answer | *Swap in your meaning and see if the sentence still makes sense
exam: «The animals heard queer sounds in the Wild Wood.» Which meaning fits best, and why? | Tasty, because the sounds are like food | *Strange, because the sounds are odd and unexpected | Happy, because the sounds are cheerful | Angry, because the animals are cross
